## Context
Arena runner lives in its own repository, while the harness still hosted analysis, reporting, protocol and open project tickets. Transfer the logical unit with evidence; retain the harness-owned routing grid and historical harness journals.

## Exit criteria
- [x] Analysis, report generators, protocol, historical reports and their tests are available in the independent arena repository with a source commit and original SHA-256 manifest.
- [x] Open arena tickets 1048, 1049, 1050, 1051, 1058, 1061, 1087, 1093 retain IDs, complete journals and unresolved criteria in arena, and leave the harness open-ticket queue.
- [x] Harness route integration points to the independent tools; routing data numbers and historical journals are unchanged.
- [x] Standalone arena tests and before/after FR+EN reproduction pass; arithmetic-correction archive hashes verify.
- [x] Harness catalog, dependency lock and full checks pass.

## Evidence
Harness: docs/arena-integration.md. Arena: migration/from-harness-2026-10-13.json and migration/README.md. Local review branches: separate-arena (harness) and separate-harness-assets (arena). Transfer does not publish or rerun private benchmark legs.
